um_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Caveat:** I can't confirm that the precise 2026 amendment text is final, and I may be misremembering the regulation and Q&A numbering. Check the current consolidated Central Bank UCITS Regulations and Q&A before relying on this.\n\n**Express 2026 approach (Reg. 26(2), as amended):**\n- **Cash vs in-kind dealing:** Cash subscriptions and redemptions may have an earlier cut-off than in-kind ones, so the fund has time to trade the underlying securities.\n- **Hedged vs unhedged classes:** Class-level currency-hedged classes may have an earlier cut-off than unhedged classes, so FX hedges can be executed.\n- **Conditions:** The cut-offs must be disclosed in the prospectus, be objectively justified, and stay before the valuation point. No forward-pricing breach or late trading is allowed.\n\n**Older Q&A 1030 approach:**\n- Equal treatment meant one dealing deadline for all classes.\n- Different deadlines needed a case-by-case derogation from the Central Bank, based on operational justification.\n- Permission came through prospectus review, not an express regulatory right.","ttft_ms":6096,"type":"result","duration_ms":9375,"uuid":"1a1c411a-b4f4-4a25-a52a-1a16e19d6f11","ttft_stream_ms":1530,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1531,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
